# PortMiami Digital Twin — browser configuration.
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Both names match the ACS project, so a key that already works
# there works here. Everything VITE_-prefixed is compiled into the browser bundle: put nothing
# secret in this file. The Google key is a *browser* key and must be restricted by HTTP referrer.
#
# Required. Google Photorealistic 3D Tiles and nothing else uses it. The key's referrer
# restriction must allow http://localhost:5200/*, or Google refuses the tiles.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Optional. Enables Cesium World Terrain beneath the tiles. The photorealistic mesh carries its
# own geometry, so the app is complete without this.
VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=
